WEBVTT

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:36.070
I want to be a part of the shut-out too.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.070
Definitely the low course!

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.780
I want to score points!

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.160
Sugi!

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.460
Mizutani, don't stop!

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.540
They dropped the ball!

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.960
Sugi, you can make it to first!

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:50.340
First base!

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:52.340
Out!

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.170
That guy... again!

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.130
Are you all right?
He's gonna hurt himself that way!

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.050
I-I-I'm fine!

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.180
I ended up out.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.010
I wanted to bring Abe home.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.770
Nice run, batter!

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.730
What a forceful voice.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.020
Who is that?

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:08.770
Um...

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.730
That's Abe's father.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.610
What!?

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.440
Beauty and the Beast, right?

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.530
Don't say that about yourself!

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.740
I'm sorry.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.990
I might have rushed it by
trying to make a double play.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.330
It's fine; it can't be helped.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.040
Don't worry about it.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.370
There's no helping it?

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:32.340
If you don't point out their mistakes, the first years will never learn!

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.050
That's why we don't get stronger.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:36.420
All right, let's finish this.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.260
Icchan, you deal with the grounders. We'll take care of the rest.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.050
Right!

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.930
First batter. First baseman: Number 5, Tajima.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:46.220
Two outs. Runners on second and third. I wanna hit!
First batter. First baseman: Number 5, Tajima.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.230
I want to let him hit!

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.140
But I can't.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.690
I can't let him hit and worsen his injury at a time like this.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.110
If it connects, it's a go?

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.480
If we see a hit, start.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.110
I'll go for the first good pitch.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.610
Two outs. Let's get the third!

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:00.910
All right.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:01.780
Got it!

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.080
First!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.540
Will this make it?

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.490
Sawa, home!

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.120
They threw to first—I can make it home!

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.420
Out!

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.960
Nice, Sawaa!

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.760
"Nice, Sawaa"? You make me sound like a drink.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.180
I'm sorry.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.850
I thought I could make it after the third baseman threw it.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:24.760
Top of the third inning. Sakitama High School to bat.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.510
I  told him to keep going, too.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.060
Going home was the right choice.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:29.980
Their first baseman was smart to have come forward and cut in on the fast throw from third.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.190
Seventh batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Harada.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.020
Now, let's turn it around with some good defense!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:36.770
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.320
Didn't think they could pull off such a play.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.490
I might have underestimated Sakitama.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:44.620
Out!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:45.580
One out!

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.030
This is bad.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:51.290
We're giving up points as usual, but we're not hitting at all.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.210
Out!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:56.880
Two outs!

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.260
If you think about it, it's that pitcher who beat Tousei.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.880
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 2, Ichihara.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.510
Even though I prepared myself for the worst,

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.470
when I look at that pitcher...

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.680
No, it couldn't have been a fluke.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.060
If it was us up against Tousei, we'd have been crushed 100 out of 100 times.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.190
Nice, right!

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:23.910
Bottom of the third inning. Nishiura High School to bat.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:24.530
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.360
Ready!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.320
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.910
It's been a while since I've done
anything but bunt. I can finally hit!

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.250
I watched his pitching style during my first at-bat. I'm going to hit it!

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.370
For now, I have to stop their first batter.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.540
Look carefully!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:34.920
I have to do my best to get rid of this
guy so it'll be advantageous for us later.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.670
Hit it! Hit it!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.250
I have to do my best to get rid of this
guy so it'll be advantageous for us later.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.420
Low course!

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.420
Right at the first pitch!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.300
Nice batting!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.260
Safe!

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.090
Don't worry about the hit!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.760
Icchan, let's retire the next batter!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.680
Strike him out!

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.180
They got their first runner on base again.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:53.600
Third batter. Third baseman: Number 8, Izumi.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.520
Will they have the third batter
bunt so the fourth can go for it?

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.820
But before, the third batter hit it too.
Third batter. Third baseman: Number 8, Izumi.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.070
Ready!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.030
Left-handed?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.110
Was he left-handed?

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.530
He was right-handed.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.870
It's a bunt. A bunt.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.580
Third! Close in.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.160
A bunt?

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.040
So the fourth batter's going to go for it
with two runners on base, like I thought?

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.540
What a pain.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.540
What's with this perfect pitch?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.470
With this, it's no outs with
runners on first and second base.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:24.970
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.470
It's time to let Hanai hit.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.550
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.430
Hit it!

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.140
Here it comes.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.810
Hitting here and bringing runners home is the fourth batter's job.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:39.860
Right, Tajima?

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.610
Tajima has nothing to do with this.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.280
Coach Momo thinks I can hit, so she's telling me to hit.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.990
It wasn't a bunt.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:49.870
Sorry about that.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.080
I'm pretty sure it wasn't your fault, Tai.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.670
But we're losing 3 to 0, and they
probably won't let Daichi hit today.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.890
Go for a double play. Take it easy!

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.420
Honestly, why are you smiling like that?

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.880
If it's a ball I like, I'll take the first pitch.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.220
Against the fourth batter of the team that beat Tousei,

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.800
considering that I've only been pitching for half a year, no matter how good a ball I throw...

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.430
Well, whatever the case, I'll throw my best ball!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:14.720
Outside low!

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.270
Out!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.440
That was close!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.280
Fifth batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Suyama.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.280
Go, Suyama!

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.040
Get your act together; we're in the middle of the game!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.370
You're the captain, aren't you?

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.880
What are you doing, just thinking about yourself?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.340
A single up the middle!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.590
Good job, Suyama!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.550
Go, go! Ah, stop, stop!

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.260
I'm the fourth batter. What am I doing?

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.390
No! I said I wouldn't do this!

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.020
One, two!

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.230
Nice batting!

00:06:58.890 --> 00:06:59.310
Sixth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Abe.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.020
Coach!

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.190
Sixth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Abe.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:04.270
Don't tell me you want to make Sakitama walk you!?

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:08.900
The worst way to give away points when the bases are loaded is with a walked-in run, right?

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.240
Ball!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.870
He slipped to the outside.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.240
What an idiot, tightening the noose around his neck.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.950
I'll wait for him to start his windup this time.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:19.910
Ball!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.960
Shit, if you're gonna do it, then do it!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.170
Ball!

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.630
It's the same as that time with Mizutani.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.670
It's the limit of this guy's courage to put in strikes.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:32.130
If their catcher would demand some strikes, he'd be able to throw them.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.600
This guy is practically useless for that sort of thing.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.060
Sakaeguchi!

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.140
I don't know what that sign means, but is this okay?

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.520
What?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.150
Is he going to do it next time for sure?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.610
Or was it some other kind of sign?

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.980
Icchan, take it easy. Bring it on!

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.400
Lucky Tai. He can relax.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.700
Being the pitcher is tiring, and having all the responsibility is exhausting.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.200
I don't want to do it anymore!

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.120
Ball four!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.500
The fielders aren't helping at all.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.210
But really, that catcher is horrible.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.470
He's not even fulfilling half of his purpose for sitting there.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.090
Timeout!

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.180
Don't worry about squeeze plays
anymore. Let's get one out at a time.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.230
Another one or two points won't make a difference.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.310
Hey...

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.940
Now's not the time to be cracking jokes.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.530
Maybe not, but there's no need to be uptight.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.940
The game is all about luck, after all.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.150
Icchan, don't!

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:37.370
If we lose today, it'll be your baseball career that ends!

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:38.830
Well...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.790
I'm sorry!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.750
It's all because I was walked!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.040
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.090
Even though everyone's trying so hard for my sake this year...

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.090
I'll hit it next time!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.340
Daichi!

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.510
We can't hear what Tai's saying!

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:58.050
It's not just for your sake, Tai.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.810
But you're always so soft. I mean...

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.680
I'm sorry, doing this mid-game...

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.770
Don't be ridiculous; I'm glad you told me.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.560
Icchan, thank you.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.440
Yeah.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.990
Well then, let's get serious from now on.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.700
Let's get some outs before they make it home!

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.320
Let's close this up!

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.410
Yeah!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.040
Icchan, you want me to be more strict?

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.580
I'm sorry for everything that's happened so far.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:28.170
Because of the trauma caused by
members who quit, I can't be strict.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:33.670
Lessening the burden on myself, and even making Icchan take on pitching—I'm really terrible.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:38.140
He said that for my sake, but today will probably be the end for me.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:39.680
All right.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.600
Today, I'll show the underclassmen my best!

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.770
It's my way of thanking
them for sticking with me!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:50.770
Bring it on!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.360
Seventh batter. Right fielder: Number 3, Oki.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.990
Shit, how embarrassing.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.200
I could've kept quiet the entire game if I'd held out for another hour.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.540
Another hour? Am I ready to lose, too?

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.290
Even if we're losing, it won't end if we don't get any outs.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.080
Baseball is tiring!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.170
Strike!

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.960
The first one went in.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.590
Seems like the timeout worked.
They'll go on without crumbling, huh?

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.180
The infielders are all drawn in.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:23.890
But Oki has already succeeded with a bunt today. It's safer than hitting.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:26.560
I'll leave the squeeze to those in the back.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:27.560
It'll hit!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.140
Here it comes!

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.520
He killed it too fast!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.940
But the catcher's jumping out.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.900
If he goes back to step on home, the other bases will...

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:34.440
Out!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.190
Daichi!

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.320
Out!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.490
What kind of arm does that guy have!?

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:42.620
Nice throw!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.240
A double play...

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.200
We were able to prevent a squeeze.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.790
We made it out of the pinch I
caused with my nervous pitches...

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.380
Icchan, nice pitch!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.380
Yeah.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:57.130
I'm not attached to pitching in the least,

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:01.890
but there's definitely a special something you can only experience on the mound.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:06.470
In this inning, with no outs and
runners on first and second base,

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.480
Hanai's at-bat ended with a right fly.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.390
Was that a bad decision?

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:14.980
Well, even if it was, this is a
game where Hanai has to hit.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:19.360
His power, competitive spirit, and good baseball skills...

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:23.950
If you put them all together, there's no mistaking that Hanai is our number two player, but...

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.740
Pitcher!

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:30.120
The gap between him and our number one is huge.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.380
If left alone, Hanai will get used to being in Tajima's shadow.
Top of the fourth inning. Sakitama High School to bat.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.130
That'd be a huge waste for both of them.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:39.460
First batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Tanaka.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:43.260
As soon as I started thinking I had to do something, Tajima sustained his injury.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:48.390
It's not what I'd call good fortune, but it makes today the perfect time to put pressure on Hanai.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.060
Left!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.350
Nice, left!

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:51.730
One out!

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.270
Second batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Sugita.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.560
One out!

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:55.440
Ready!

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.900
Second batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Sugita.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.280
One out. We're still okay.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.110
With me, Atsushi, and Tai, we can fill the bases.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.820
You won't be able to walk Daichi if that happens!

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:07.910
Strike!

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.490
You're swinging too hard!

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.040
Sugita, fight! Don't swing around!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:16.630
I know, but with my strength, I can't get it past the infield if I don't swing as hard as I can.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.840
If I can reach it, I'll swing.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.630
One, two. Nice batting!

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:22.630
Nice batting!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:25.050
All right! From now on, we're going to fight back!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:29.140
One out!

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:31.680
Well, that's fine.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.060
As long as we can end this inning with four batters, the top of the fifth inning will be Sakura.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.100
Third batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Furusawa.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:38.570
If possible, I want to go up against Sakura today.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.150
Bunt... Middle high.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.200
Fastball.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:48.700
Out!

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:50.700
It flew up, huh?

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:52.410
I'm sorry.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:52.870
Fourth batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Oyama.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.210
It's fine. There's no helping it.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.120
Fourth batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Oyama.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.670
It's nothing...

00:12:58.880 --> 00:12:59.710
Ready!

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:05.510
"There's no helping it" has kind of become a habit.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.970
Well, I'll apologize to everyone after the game for being too soft,

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.930
but for now, I have to get on first base.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:14.350
A fastball right there.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.150
Strike!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.730
Yeah, I can hit this.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.110
But I better be careful here.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.320
He doesn't stand out because of Sakura,

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.070
but Oyama has also handled his position as fourth batter well in the past two games.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.080
Just in case, we should let one ball loose.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:31.830
Curve.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:35.120
Ball.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.370
Was that a curve just now?

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.830
Well, the type of pitch doesn't matter.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.590
Up high.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.090
High!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.220
Is he waiting for a pitch on the inside?

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.220
It'll be a pain if he sticks around hitting fouls.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.260
We'll throw it where you want, so hit it!

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.600
From a strike to a ball.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:52.560
Here it comes. Inside high!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.270
A shootball!

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.600
It hit on the handle. Ow, my hands are numb!

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.730
Shit!

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:01.440
There's no call.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.860
Tai!

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:05.070
Tai, you're safe! Nice batting!

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.910
Really? They didn't get me out?

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.870
It looks like the bound was high and the ball wouldn't drop easily.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:13.870
All right!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.080
Two outs. Runners on first and second base, and now Daichi.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.750
Third base is open, so if he hits a single, it'll stop at one run.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.790
Even if he hits a home run, it won't even the score!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.790
Even if he hits a home run, it won't even the score!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.090
Two outs!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.050
Ready!

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.840
You don't need to load the bases, right?!

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.050
Don't stand, catcher!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.260
It's too dangerous with two runners on base.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.430
No good, huh...

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.640
There's no heckling this time.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.190
Before...

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.400
Well, of course.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:46.190
They're loading the bases.
There's no reason to complain.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.990
I thought the heckling from before was strange, too.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.660
It's just not appropriate for high school baseball,

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:54.910
like when people use the "just one more" chant when there are two outs.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.000
Just as I thought. They were heckled, weren't they?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.790
If they're so frustrated, then tell the sixth batter to hit it!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.540
Well, even if you say that, you know...

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.840
The one bearing the full brunt of it is the pitcher, right?

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:05.750
I'm so sorry.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.460
Not at all.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.920
Baseball is really complicated, after all.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:11.220
Ball four.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.890
Sixth batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Kamimura.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:15.680
We have two outs, but the bases are loaded.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:19.100
Ryou, please hit! The bases are loaded!

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.560
Let's at least put up one point!

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.190
It flew up!

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:25.900
Out!

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.900
Getting runners on base before Daichi, and then returning them with Daichi.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:32.070
It was working for us before, but now...

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:35.910
If Daichi is walked, the batting order starts to work against us.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.580
Tai!

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.500
Even though I said I would hit the next time...

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:42.960
Don't cry.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.540
There's nothing you can do about being walked, right?

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.800
Right.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.300
Our loss is becoming more of a reality.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:52.880
We can't score any runs.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:55.510
Bottom of the fourth inning. Nishiura High School to bat.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.930
This development shows how long we've been playing baseball without thinking things through.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:03.190
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.020
Ready!

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:08.980
Having realized that, my
options still haven't changed.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:12.610
I can only keep pitching as usual, trying to cut off their attack!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.360
A fastball!

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:16.370
A hit to right field!

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.830
We're on base. This time, we'll score more efficiently.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:20.410
Before we get back to the first batter, I'd like to get one out.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:23.330
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.330
I'll hold them down to zero runs in this inning

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.750
Have to get it to roll.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.380
Catcher!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.130
Yes!

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:31.710
Out!

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:36.180
Mihashi!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.350
I'll make up for that bunt right now with my legs.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.100
Don't "strictly" get depressed!

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.350
Yeah!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.560
One out with a runner on first base. We're still okay.

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:50.020
First batter. First baseman: Number 5, Tajima.
Sakitama isn't moving their fielders forward.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:51.900
I'll take care of the first one with a strike!

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.320
We've got one out.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.990
I'll end this inning before it gets around to the clean-up hitter.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:57.660
Again!?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.830
Here comes the third baseman!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:00.990
First!
This time, I'll definitely...

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.210
Mizutani, take third base!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.710
Sugi, don't worry about it!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.550
I'm sorry.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:14.220
It's that guy's third safety bunt, after all. I understand why you feel impatient.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:18.180
Shit! Why does he keep bunting?

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.050
He was the fourth batter in the previous match, right?

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:24.930
If I remember right, his records of outfield hits and strikeouts were all fitting for a fourth batter.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:28.690
And he played third base, but for some reason, he's on first today...

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.060
An injury?

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:32.860
I'd wondered why his position changed,

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:36.360
but if there was a reason they had to move him from third to first base, then...

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.660
The original left-handed first
baseman became a right fielder.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:42.620
Due to prior infield experience, they put the center fielder on third base.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.330
The captain, who was their right fielder, took over center field.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:48.170
It fits pretty nicely if that's the case, doesn't it?

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.670
Let's go!

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:51.960
If I... had made the bunt,
we would've scored a run, right?

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:57.590
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.720
Mihashi! Is that bunt from before bothering you?

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.100
Be positive!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.470
Y-Yeah. I'll think positively.

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:05.310
Ball!

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:10.690
Tajima was going to make up for my part with his legs.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.110
Sakaeguchi, keep going!

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.070
Tajima, good luck.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:17.860
Tajima.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.870
Tajima? Not "Sakaeguchi, good luck"?

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.830
Okay! No strikes, two balls.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:25.660
Damn it. Trickling in one after another...

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:29.670
Safe!

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:31.830
Pitcher! Compete with the batter!

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:38.300
You say that, but you'll throw it to second base if he runs, won't you?

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:41.260
When you do that, the third
runner will definitely come home.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.810
If we make any mistakes, it'll be one run even if they don't hit the ball.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:47.600
Icchan,

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:49.810
it's all right to fill the bases.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.940
But the third batter is next.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.020
In the first inning, he got three bases after hitting.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:58.400
However, we were able to get a double
play when the bases were loaded before.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:01.030
I don't have to worry about
squeeze plays or stolen bases either.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:06.120
When the other team is leading, Icchan's ability to process information is halved.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.700
Wanting to get a head-start, we took the first offense,

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:11.000
but it's the worst when the opposition has the lead.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.710
Ball! Ball four!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.710
Did they really just fill the bases,

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:19.420
even though Izumi, who's hit
two out of two today, is next?

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.680
Third batter. Third baseman: Number 8, Izumi.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:21.680
Sakaeguchi!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:22.340
Yeah?

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:23.970
Take a big lead, okay?

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:24.680
Yeah.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:39.320
More!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.610
Come out more!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.950
Yeah, right there!

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:48.490
With one out and the bases loaded, the first base runner should stand there.

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:51.000
If they try for a pickoff, we'll be the lucky ones.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.750
But, even if you know that, it's scary to stand out so far.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.960
Now then, let's get some runs in.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.420
Even if it's an outfield fly, it's one run.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.710
Yes!

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.760
Um...

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.760
That's right.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.050
For this guy, I'll make the first pitch a screwball!

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:09.310
Strike!

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:10.100
It went in.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.640
Nice pitch!

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.440
Will another one come?

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:17.320
Step in with the timing of the fastball, and if it's a screw, match up to it with my arms.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:19.320
One run with an outfield fly.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.320
I'll leave the remaining runners to Hanai.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.070
His bat stopped.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:24.820
Let's try continuing with another screwball.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.490
Make it feel like I'm putting it at the outside.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.990
Another screwball!

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:28.780
Strike!

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:30.290
He swung this time.

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.080
I was cornered.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.830
If the next one comes with the same course, it'll be scary.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.130
I want to avoid another double
play while the bases are loaded.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.630
Izumi. Third runner!

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.920
I don't need your sheepish grin.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:46.470
However, I don't feel as relaxed as I should from looking at the third runner.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:47.800
Okay.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:50.140
I'll go with the same approach as the second pitch.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:50.930
The timing...

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:51.810
...was right.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.480
I'll mix in a fastball. It's two strikes, no balls.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:57.480
Don't think about control too much.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.400
A fast pitch!

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:00.070
A fastball! Hit it as-is!

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:02.280
All right. Let's go for a double play!

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:04.070
Safe!

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:05.740
They got one run! At least first base...!

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.360
Out!

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.320
Sawa, home!

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:08.070
Seriously!?

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:08.820
Second's runner is coming!

00:21:08.820 --> 00:21:10.700
Right! Right!
Tajima, slide!

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.080
Safe! Safe!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.040
Our sixth run!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:17.750
Tajima!

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.460
Hey, I'm back!

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.500
See?

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.760
Awesome...

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.340
Wait just a moment.

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.470
Yes?

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.800
It's fine to run when you can run,

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.720
but what you just did was pretty dangerous.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.430
There are times when you should run even if it's dangerous,

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:36.480
as well as times when you should wait on base.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:37.190
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:38.350
Sorry.

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:40.060
Why are you apologizing, Mihashi?

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.820
It really was pretty close.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:47.200
It's Tajima, so he probably did it
because he had a chance for success.

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:49.990
Because Coach Momo said it in such a way.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:53.120
Is it... because I'm not... reliable?

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.080
Tajima, good luck!

00:21:56.790 --> 00:22:00.000
Even while injured, Tajima is being relied on more?

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.880
Aren't I the fourth batter today?

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.220
Nishiura is winning.

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:46.150
Hanai, who isn't satisfied with his performance as fourth batter,

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:48.030
seems to be anguishing on his own.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:51.450
In contrast with Hanai, as expected of Tajima...

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:54.070
Even if he can't hit, he accomplishes a lot!

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:55.530
Tajima is amazing, after all!

00:23:55.870 --> 00:24:01.660
But Tajima's accomplishments seem to put further pressure on Hanai instead.

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:06.040
I wonder if Hanai can grasp something in today's game.

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:07.040
Next time:

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:08.300
I Want to Play Baseball.

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:10.550
It's the conclusion to the third round!
